  Lab Grown Diamond Bracelets A bracelet is one of the few pieces of jewellery worn every day, through work, travel, and everything in between. Lucira's lab grown diamond bracelets are built for that kind of wear: real diamonds, grown in a lab rather than mined from the earth, set in 14KT, 18KT, or 9KT gold, and certified for clarity and authenticity. From tennis bracelets that catch the light in a continuous line to delicate chain and mangalsutra styles, this collection covers the everyday and the occasion piece alike. Why Choose a Lab Grown Diamond Bracelet Lab grown diamonds are chemically, physically, and optically identical to mined diamonds. The only difference is origin: one forms over geological time underground, the other forms in a controlled lab environment using CVD or HPHT technology. Because the production process is more efficient, lab grown diamonds typically cost less than a mined diamond of comparable cut, clarity, and carat, which is why a genuine diamond bracelet has become more accessible without a change in quality or durability. At Lucira, every lab grown diamond bracelet is disclosed as lab grown, never presented as anything else, and comes with certification that verifies the diamond's grading. Shop by Style Tennis Bracelets A continuous line of diamonds set edge to edge, the tennis bracelet is Lucira's most requested bracelet style for everyday wear. For our full tennis bracelet range, see the lab grown diamond tennis bracelet collection. Chain Bracelets Lighter and more versatile, chain bracelets pair diamonds with delicate gold links for a piece that layers well with other jewellery. Mangalsutra Bracelets A modern take on a traditional symbol, the mangalsutra bracelet brings diamonds and gold into a design meant for daily wear rather than occasion-only use. Men's Bracelets Structured, geometric, and set in solid gold, Lucira's men's bracelets apply the same certification and craftsmanship standards to a bolder silhouette. Lab Grown Diamond Bracelet Price Guide Price depends on total carat weight, diamond shape, gold karatage, and setting style. Simple prong-set styles in 14KT gold sit at the accessible end of the range, while higher carat tennis bracelets in 18KT gold with bezel settings sit higher. Prices are subject to change based on prevailing gold rates. How to Choose the Right Lab Grown Diamond Bracelet Start with how often you plan to wear it. For daily wear, a lower profile prong or bezel setting in 14KT gold resists everyday knocks well. For occasion pieces, a higher carat tennis bracelet or a bracelet with fancy-shape diamonds makes more of a statement. Wrist size matters too: most Lucira bracelets are available from 5 inch to 7 inch lengths, and our sizing guide on each product page can help you confirm fit before ordering. Certification and Trust Every lab grown diamond bracelet at Lucira is IGI or SGL certified, and all gold is BIS hallmarked. Lucira also offers a 90% lifetime buyback and 100% lifetime exchange on eligible pieces, along with in-person support at our experience centres in Mumbai, Pune, and Noida. Frequently Asked Questions Is a lab grown diamond bracelet worth buying?Yes, for buyers who want genuine diamond brilliance without the premium of a mined stone. Lab grown diamonds offer the same hardness, sparkle, and durability as mined diamonds at a comparatively lower price point, making them a practical choice for everyday jewellery. How much does a lab grown diamond bracelet cost?Cost depends on carat weight, diamond shape, gold karatage, and setting complexity. Simpler designs in 14KT gold sit at the lower end, while higher carat tennis bracelets in 18KT gold cost more. Exact pricing is available on each product page and is subject to change based on gold rates. How do I clean a lab grown diamond bracelet?Use lukewarm water with a mild soap, a soft-bristle brush for gentle cleaning around the setting, and a soft cloth to dry. Avoid harsh chemicals and remove the bracelet before swimming or exercising. What carat weight should I choose for a bracelet?For everyday wear, lower total carat weight in a secure prong or bezel setting tends to hold up better against daily knocks. For occasion wear, a higher carat tennis bracelet makes more of a visual statement. Does Lucira offer buyback or exchange on bracelets?Yes, eligible Lucira bracelets come with a 90% lifetime buyback and 100% lifetime exchange policy. Terms are confirmed at the time of purchase and may vary by collection.
